---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import EffectRow from '../components/EffectRow.astro';
import { stats, reconciliation } from '../lib/data';
import { u, pct, int } from '../lib/fmt';

const s = stats();
const o = s.overall;
const c = s.counts;
const pr = s.predictors;
const rr = reconciliation();
const ar = rr.counts.retested_addition_bibliographic_relations;
const additionsAlreadyInForrt = (ar.exact_expression_pair_reported ?? 0)
  + (ar.reviewed_same_work_pair_expression_unresolved ?? 0)
  + (ar.reviewed_same_work_pair_versioned_expressions ?? 0);
// 100-cell waffle: the whole record at a glance
const cells = (() => {
  const ok = Math.round((o.successful / o.n) * 100), mix = Math.round((o.mixed / o.n) * 100);
  return [...Array(ok).fill('ok'), ...Array(mix).fill('mix'), ...Array(100 - ok - mix).fill('bad')];
})();
---
<Base title="Retested">
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div class="hgrid">
      <div class="htext rise">
        <div class="label">The record, as of the latest build</div>
        <h1>Psychology tested its famous findings <em>again.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">Of <b class="num">{int(o.n)}</b> replication attempts with a verdict, <b class="obs">{pct(o.success_share)}</b> found the original effect. <b class="mixc">{pct(o.mixed / o.n)}</b> were mixed. <b class="claim">{pct(o.failed / o.n)}</b> did not find it.</p>
        <p class="sub muted">Retested follows each finding from the original claim to every attempt to repeat it: what the replicators said, what the numbers show, and how the attempts were run.</p>
        <div class="cta">
          <a class="btn" href={u('game/')}>Play: did it replicate? →</a>
          <a class="btn ghost" href={u('effects/')}>Browse {c.effects} effects</a>
        </div>
        <p class="game-note faint">Start with today’s ten: make a probability call about each real finding, see what later studies reported, then share your score. No account needed.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="waffle rise" aria-label={`Of every 100 replications: ${cells.filter((x) => x === 'ok').length} replicated, ${cells.filter((x) => x === 'mix').length} mixed, ${cells.filter((x) => x === 'bad').length} did not.`}>
        <div class="cells">{cells.map((t, i) => <i class={t} style={`--d:${i * 9}ms`}></i>)}</div>
        <figcaption class="mono"><span><i class="ok"></i>replicated</span><span><i class="mix"></i>mixed</span><span><i class="bad"></i>did not</span><span class="faint">each square = 1% of {int(o.n)} attempts</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="sh"><h2>Three things the record shows</h2><span class="label">computed from coded study data</span></div>
    <div class="grid grid-3 facts">
      <article>
        <div class="fig2"><b class="obs">{pct(pr.p_le_005.success_share)}</b><span>vs</span><b class="claim">{pct(pr.p_005_05.success_share)}</b></div>
        <h3>A strong p-value predicts survival</h3>
        <p>Originals with p ≤ .005 replicated {pct(pr.p_le_005.success_share)} of the time; those that only just cleared p &lt; .05 did so {pct(pr.p_005_05.success_share)} of the time. <span class="faint">n = {pr.p_le_005.n} and {pr.p_005_05.n} original studies.</span></p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <div class="fig2"><b class="claim">{pct(pr.overlapping_authors.success_share)}</b><span>vs</span><b class="obs">{pct(pr.independent_team.success_share)}</b></div>
        <h3>Who replicates matters</h3>
        <p>When a replication team shared authors with the original, it succeeded {pct(pr.overlapping_authors.success_share)} of the time. Fully independent teams: {pct(pr.independent_team.success_share)}. <span class="faint">n = {pr.overlapping_authors.n} and {pr.independent_team.n} attempts.</span></p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <div class="fig2"><b class="claim">{Math.round(s.shrinkage.median_ratio * 100)}%</b></div>
        <h3>Even survivors shrink</h3>
        <p>The typical replication found an effect {Math.round(s.shrinkage.median_ratio * 100)}% the size of the original's. {pct(s.shrinkage.share_below_half)} came in below half; {pct(s.shrinkage.share_sign_flip)} pointed the other way. <span class="faint">{s.shrinkage.n_rows} effects with sizes on both sides.</span></p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="faint caveat">These are rates among studies people chose to replicate, which are often the surprising or doubted ones. They are not the replication rate of psychology as a whole. <a href={u('stats/')}>See the full record and its caveats.</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap grid grid-2 doors">
    <div>
      <div class="sh"><h2>The Graveyard</h2><a class="label" href={u('graveyard/')}>top {s.lists.graveyard.length} →</a></div>
      <ul class="rowlist">{s.lists.graveyard.slice(0, 7).map((e) => <EffectRow e={e} showFame />)}</ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="sh"><h2>The Survivors</h2><a class="label" href={u('survivors/')}>top {s.lists.survivors.length} →</a></div>
      <ul class="rowlist">{s.lists.survivors.filter((e) => e.record.k > 0).slice(0, 7).map((e) => <EffectRow e={e} showFame />)}</ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="band card">
      <div>
        <div class="label claim">Source checked by Retested</div>
        <h2>{int(c.retested_new_effects)} completed effect pages added to this site</h2>
        <p>{int(c.retested_new_findings)} original papers and {int(c.retested_new_pairs)} source-reviewed replication pairs were added to Retested's built record. Of those pairs, {int(additionsAlreadyInForrt)} already have positive bibliographic same-pair evidence in the frozen FORRT comparison. The rest are unresolved comparisons, not certified first discoveries. Each page links the original claim to the later study and shows the reported result.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="band-actions"><a class="btn ghost" href={u('effects/?source=retested')}>Browse the additions →</a><a class="btn ghost" href={u('coverage/')}>Audit the overlap →</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="band card ink">
      <div>
        <div class="label claim">Extending the record</div>
        <h2>{int(c.candidates)} candidate records awaiting Retested source checks</h2>
        <p>FORRT's extractor and Retested's search have flagged papers that look like replications. FORRT already records an outcome for some of them. The queue count means Retested has not yet checked the exact study link, participants, and reported result for a completed page.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="btn" href={u('queue/')}>Open the review queue →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem); padding-bottom: 2rem; }
  .hgrid { display: grid; gap: 3rem; align-items: center; }
  @media (min-width: 960px) { .hgrid { grid-template-columns: 1.25fr 1fr; } }
  .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 6.4vw, 5.2rem); line-height: 1; margin: .7rem 0 1.4rem; }
  .hero h1 em { color: var(--claim); font-variation-settings: "SOFT" 100, "WONK" 1; }
  .lede { font: 400 clamp(1.2rem, 2vw, 1.5rem)/1.45 var(--f-display); }
  .lede b { font-weight: 600; }
  .mixc { color: var(--mix); }
  .sub { font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .8rem; margin-top: 1.6rem; }
  .game-note { font-size: .82rem; margin: .7rem 0 0; max-width: 60ch; }
  .waffle .cells { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(10, 1fr); gap: 5px; max-width: 420px; }
  .waffle .cells i { aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 2px; display: block; }
  .waffle i.ok { background: var(--ok); } .waffle i.mix { background: var(--mix); } .waffle i.bad { background: transparent; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--bad); }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) { .waffle .cells i { animation: pop .5s both; animation-delay: var(--d); } @keyframes pop { from { transform: scale(0); } to { transform: none; } } }
  .waffle figcaption { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .4rem 1rem; font-size: .72rem; margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .waffle figcaption i { display: inline-block; width: 10px; height: 10px; margin-right: .35rem; vertical-align: -1px; border-radius: 2px; }
  .facts article { border-top: 3px solid var(--ink); padding-top: 1rem; }
  .fig2 { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: .6rem; font: 500 clamp(2.4rem, 4.5vw, 3.4rem)/1 var(--f-display); margin-bottom: .8rem; }
  .fig2 span { font: .8rem var(--f-mono); color: var(--ink-3); }
  .caveat { font-size: .9rem; margin-top: 1.2rem; }
  .doors .sh a { text-decoration: none; }
  .band { display: grid; gap: 1.5rem; align-items: center; margin-top: 4rem; }
  @media (min-width: 860px) { .band { grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; } }
  .band h2 { margin: .4rem 0 .6rem; }
  .band-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .65rem; }
</style>
